        "content": "<p>jrandolf opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14830\">issue #14830</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>bindgen!</code> emits <code>std::collections::HashMap&lt;K, V&gt;</code> for <code>map&lt;K, V&gt;</code>, but Wasmtime only implements <code>ComponentType</code>/<code>Lift</code>/<code>Lower</code> for the <code>HashMap</code> behind its internal <code>hash_map</code> alias, which is <code>hashbrown::HashMap</code> when wasmtime's <code>std</code> feature is off. So any WIT using <code>map</code> fails to compile with, for example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"TOML\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">version</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"...\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default-features</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">features</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"runtime\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"component-model\"</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">component</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">bindgen</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">({</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"package a:b; interface i { f: func(m: map&lt;string, u32&gt;); } world w { import i; }\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">E0277</span><span class=\"p\">]:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">trait</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">`</span><span class=\"n\">ComponentType</span><span class=\"err\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">implemented</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">`</span><span class=\"n\">HashMap</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nb\">String</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u32</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"err\">`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The generated path also doesn't go through <code>wasmtime_crate</code>/<code>__internal</code> like <code>Vec</code> and <code>String</code> do, so it doesn't work from <code>#![no_std]</code> crates either. The existing <code>codegen_no_std.rs</code> test doesn't catch this since it re-adds <code>extern crate std</code> and builds wasmtime with default features.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633106992,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792437208
    },
